# World 3, the Highlands (SPEC 13; docs/STYLE-world3.md): the hardware pilot. Ctrl+L, W, 7 starts mission 7 (Foothills) behind its
# card; disk/world3.bin loads into the world arena there (replacing the previous world's art), the terrain strip's ring fills under
# the card (1 column a picture, behind a blank strip), then the chopper takes off from the pad and flies east along the pass:
# - lines 24-129: the sky gradient (COLOR00 a line), the far range (88-129) at 1/4;
# - lines 130-255: the terrain strip, 1:1, a 16 px column streamed in as the camera moves, the haze gradient behind it;
# The same flight is the world's frame budget: no dropped frames.
wait-serial "AGK t0" 1000
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x11
wait 5
key 0x07
wait-serial "AGK world 3 loaded" 400
wait 60
screenshot card
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x02
wait 40
screenshot start
# the pilot's own pixels: the sky's top (SPEC 13.3: 236), the far range's pens, the strip's rock (pens 2, 3, 1 of M7)
expect-color start 60 100 0x9AC
expect-color start 10 105 0x568
expect-color start 4 250 0x765
expect-color start 100 240 0x435
expect-color start 300 200 0x112
press up 40
hold right
wait 100
screenshot fly1
wait 100
screenshot fly2
wait 100
screenshot fly3
wait 100
screenshot fly4
release
press fire 10
wait 30
screenshot end
expect-serial "AGK start world=3 mission=7"
expect-serial "AGK world=3 mission=7"
expect-serial "world3 copper_used=\d+ copper_max=\d+"
expect-no-serial "ERR|missing"
expect-no-dropped-frames
expect-max-load 85
expect-min-chip-free 96
